WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.010
- What's up Believe Nation.

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:06.011
My name is Evan, my one word is believe,

00:00:06.011 --> 00:00:07.884
and I believe in people more than

00:00:07.884 --> 00:00:09.309
they believe in themselves,

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:12.360
and my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.300
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.684
And so to help you on your journey,

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.503
I started the Best of Tony
series as an experiment,

00:00:20.503 --> 00:00:23.809
as a test. Tony Robbins
has had an impact on me,

00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:25.558
and a lot of the viewers on my channel,

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.552
and so I thought maybe once a month,

00:00:27.552 --> 00:00:30.805
maybe bring some of his best
content that I really enjoyed

00:00:30.805 --> 00:00:34.062
to inspire, enlighten, motivate you.

00:00:34.062 --> 00:00:36.012
And so today we're going to
learn from Tony about how

00:00:36.012 --> 00:00:39.186
he turned somebody who
had a lifelong stutter

00:00:39.186 --> 00:00:42.190
that really held him back in
life and he turned it around

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.226
and transformed the man's life as well.

00:00:44.226 --> 00:00:45.643
I hope you enjoy.

00:00:48.209 --> 00:00:50.376
- My name is Rechaud Bell.

00:00:55.122 --> 00:00:58.872
I've stuttered for as
long as I can remember.

00:01:04.344 --> 00:01:08.511
My freshman year of college,
one of the first courses I took

00:01:11.464 --> 00:01:14.047
was a speech class and I froze.

00:01:17.974 --> 00:01:20.474
The grade I received was an F.

00:01:21.755 --> 00:01:25.922
I went from a full time
college student on scholarship

00:01:28.807 --> 00:01:32.974
to stocking shelves on the
graveyard shift at minimum wage.

00:01:40.512 --> 00:01:44.679
The industry I'm in is
basically a sales industry,

00:01:46.415 --> 00:01:50.582
and stuttering has gotten in
the way of closing a deal,

00:01:54.426 --> 00:01:58.130
or even to schedule an appointment.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.297
I could have a more successful
career if I spoke fluently.

00:02:08.223 --> 00:02:09.969
- Tony it would mean so much to me

00:02:09.969 --> 00:02:12.003
if you could help
Rechaud with his stutter.

00:02:12.003 --> 00:02:13.753
He is such an incredible man,

00:02:13.753 --> 00:02:17.987
and I know there is so much
more potential that he has.

00:02:17.987 --> 00:02:20.025
Everyday is a struggle for him.

00:02:20.025 --> 00:02:22.182
His stutter holds him back a lot,

00:02:22.182 --> 00:02:24.765
and makes him question himself.

00:02:25.604 --> 00:02:29.756
It's so hard, because I
can't do anything about it.

00:02:29.756 --> 00:02:31.302
Tony, if you could help,

00:02:31.302 --> 00:02:35.469
that would just mean so much
to me and to our family.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.611
- Rechaud, nice to meet you.

00:02:43.611 --> 00:02:44.594
- Nice to meet you too.

00:02:44.594 --> 00:02:45.891
- Well, tell me a little
bit, if you would,

00:02:45.891 --> 00:02:47.192
about what's going on in your life.

00:02:47.192 --> 00:02:49.628
I understand you're having
difficulty in terms of

00:02:49.628 --> 00:02:51.530
a speech impediment or stuttering.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:54.947
- I just know, and my life I rejected it.

00:03:02.131 --> 00:03:03.798
I was ashamed of it.

00:03:06.851 --> 00:03:11.018
I drew back and was extremely
introverted, but accepted.

00:03:18.841 --> 00:03:20.427
- You've gone through several stages

00:03:20.427 --> 00:03:22.338
that are perfect stages.

00:03:22.338 --> 00:03:23.879
You've gone through ashamed,

00:03:23.879 --> 00:03:25.628
you've gone through rejection,

00:03:25.628 --> 00:03:27.702
and you've gone through acceptance.

00:03:27.702 --> 00:03:29.491
You've accepted this experience.

00:03:29.491 --> 00:03:32.912
Now that you've accepted
it, you can eliminate it.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.552
- Yeah. Sign me up for that right now.

00:03:35.552 --> 00:03:36.892
- Okay, now I want you to
notice what you just said.

00:03:36.892 --> 00:03:38.233
Do that exactly like you said.

00:03:38.233 --> 00:03:39.416
Yeah, sign me up for that right now.

00:03:39.416 --> 00:03:40.249
Say that again.

00:03:40.249 --> 00:03:42.288
- Yeah. Sign me up for that right now.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.912
- Now you just spoke perfectly.

00:03:43.912 --> 00:03:44.856
Now there were other parts of your speech

00:03:44.856 --> 00:03:46.322
that were perfect as well,

00:03:46.322 --> 00:03:50.026
but you just demonstrated
what I'm going to show you.

00:03:50.026 --> 00:03:51.096
It's hard as human beings to figure out

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:52.601
what makes people do what they do.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:56.060
But because I spent 30
years in a 100 countries,

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.701
with more than three and
a half million people,

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:00.489
at this point I could be an
idiot and I'd have to see

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:02.644
there's patterns that make people crazy,

00:04:02.644 --> 00:04:05.248
that make people happy,
that make them fulfilled,

00:04:05.248 --> 00:04:07.195
that make them stutter.

00:04:07.195 --> 00:04:11.362
Once you know what the pattern
is, it's so easy to change.

00:04:13.006 --> 00:04:16.422
Almost every unconscious
pattern happened a long time ago

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.493
when we make a decision about something.

00:04:18.493 --> 00:04:20.162
We model something.

00:04:20.162 --> 00:04:23.460
We model a behavior or
we reject a behavior.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.575
Deep in our unconscious
it becomes a pattern

00:04:25.575 --> 00:04:28.012
to avoid pain or to gain pleasure.

00:04:28.012 --> 00:04:30.205
When did you start stuttering?

00:04:30.205 --> 00:04:31.788
Tell me the moment.

00:04:33.175 --> 00:04:35.571
What's your earliest memory?

00:04:35.571 --> 00:04:38.416
What's your earliest memory in life?

00:04:38.416 --> 00:04:40.205
Take a moment.

00:04:40.205 --> 00:04:42.622
Your earliest memory in life.

00:04:44.638 --> 00:04:48.471
- Probably two years
old, get up on a Saturday

00:04:51.392 --> 00:04:54.365
watching cartoons and eating cereal.

00:04:54.365 --> 00:04:57.532
I believe it was Rocky and Bullwinkle.

00:05:00.872 --> 00:05:04.289
- And Bullwinkle, does he have a stutter?

00:05:05.673 --> 00:05:06.673
R-r-r-rocky?

00:05:08.853 --> 00:05:09.686
- Wow.

00:05:11.654 --> 00:05:14.487
- And that's your earliest memory.

00:05:16.296 --> 00:05:18.659
And when Bullwinkle
got himself in trouble,

00:05:18.659 --> 00:05:20.083
how did he get out of
trouble when somebody was

00:05:20.083 --> 00:05:23.251
going to like torture him
or do something bad to him?

00:05:23.251 --> 00:05:27.157
- He would scream out,
'R-r-r-rocky,' right?

00:05:27.157 --> 00:05:30.657
- And he always stuttered when he said it.

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:36.147
So I want you to do this,

00:05:36.147 --> 00:05:38.304
all patterns like that
happen because you've

00:05:38.304 --> 00:05:41.353
forgotten something
right before that moment.

00:05:41.353 --> 00:05:43.146
And now you're locked in by the pattern.

00:05:43.146 --> 00:05:45.875
There's the decision you made
or something you experienced,

00:05:45.875 --> 00:05:50.433
or life was very different
right before that moment.

00:05:50.433 --> 00:05:52.403
Go back to right before that moment,

00:05:52.403 --> 00:05:56.070
and I want you to
recapture what you forgot.

00:05:59.964 --> 00:06:02.881
- My parents were probably arguing.

00:06:05.009 --> 00:06:07.700
That was happening quite often.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.533
- Yes.

00:06:08.533 --> 00:06:12.366
- Like to the point where
my dad got physical.

00:06:13.987 --> 00:06:16.966
- And you didn't know what to do, did ya?

00:06:16.966 --> 00:06:19.549
- Needed clarity and assurance.

00:06:21.443 --> 00:06:24.184
- Yeah. And did you get it?

00:06:24.184 --> 00:06:28.017
- I guess I got that
from, 'Hey, R-r-r-rocky.'

00:06:32.929 --> 00:06:35.775
- Because the one thing
Rocky always responded to was

00:06:35.775 --> 00:06:36.608
- Help.

00:06:38.259 --> 00:06:42.426
- But not just a cry for help,
a stuttering cry for help.

00:06:44.564 --> 00:06:46.881
Even a child who can't
consciously understand that

00:06:46.881 --> 00:06:49.076
he feels helpless will
find a way to intervene

00:06:49.076 --> 00:06:52.752
and stop pain going
between those he loves.

00:06:52.752 --> 00:06:56.209
And one of the ways to do
that is create a new problem.

00:06:56.209 --> 00:06:58.202
So you found a way to protect your mother,

00:06:58.202 --> 00:07:01.696
stop your father from
beating her, and it worked.

00:07:01.696 --> 00:07:03.526
That was perfect for a two year old.

00:07:03.526 --> 00:07:05.906
Not good for a 30 year old Rechaud.

00:07:05.906 --> 00:07:06.965
- Right.

00:07:06.965 --> 00:07:09.465
- So now what? Do we stay two?

00:07:10.871 --> 00:07:14.704
- No. No we don't stay
two. We don't stay two.

00:07:16.894 --> 00:07:18.096
- You're a man, you're 30 years old.

00:07:18.096 --> 00:07:20.703
You've lived life. You've been
through all kinds of stuff.

00:07:20.703 --> 00:07:23.958
There's a warrior in you Rechaud.

00:07:23.958 --> 00:07:25.865
Feel him and where he is.

00:07:25.865 --> 00:07:27.568
Breathe him in.

00:07:27.568 --> 00:07:29.724
The warrior is one that can face anything

00:07:29.724 --> 00:07:30.941
and storm through it.

00:07:30.941 --> 00:07:32.203
Warrior, once he sets his mind to it,

00:07:32.203 --> 00:07:34.566
he will do whatever battle is necessary,

00:07:34.566 --> 00:07:36.723
for his wife, for his family, for himself.

00:07:36.723 --> 00:07:38.107
Make the sound of the warrior,

00:07:38.107 --> 00:07:39.492
the first sound that comes to you.

00:07:39.492 --> 00:07:40.891
Make the sound, make the
sound of the warrior.

00:07:40.891 --> 00:07:43.667
- (screams)

00:07:43.667 --> 00:07:46.594
- The warrior does not stutter. Ever.

00:07:46.594 --> 00:07:47.978
Own the warrior.

00:07:47.978 --> 00:07:50.095
- (screams)

00:07:50.095 --> 00:07:51.856
- Tell me what the warrior says. Now.

00:07:51.856 --> 00:07:53.445
- The warrior says I am free.

00:07:53.445 --> 00:07:54.990
- The warrior says ...

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.942
- The warrior says, I am brilliant.

00:07:56.942 --> 00:07:58.445
- That's right. The warrior says ...

00:07:58.445 --> 00:08:00.399
- The warrior says that I am electric.

00:08:00.399 --> 00:08:01.741
- The warrior says ...

00:08:01.741 --> 00:08:03.165
- I am awesome.

00:08:03.165 --> 00:08:05.485
- Ask the warrior, do I
need to stutter anymore?

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:06.318
- No.

00:08:14.072 --> 00:08:15.489
That was awesome.

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:18.483
- You're awesome.

00:08:18.483 --> 00:08:20.022
- Thank you, Thank you. Wow.

00:08:20.022 --> 00:08:21.816
So, what's next coach?

00:08:21.816 --> 00:08:24.599
(laughter)

00:08:24.599 --> 00:08:28.766
(audience applause and whistling)

00:08:31.098 --> 00:08:34.454
- Give him a hand. Rechaud,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:08:34.454 --> 00:08:37.665
Rechaud. Give it up for Rechaud.

00:08:37.665 --> 00:08:38.832
- Oooooh, yes.

00:08:55.584 --> 00:08:58.690
Just a quick question.
Just a quick question.

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:00.400
Would you just share, Rechaud.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.533
What was going on before,
and what had changed for you?

00:09:03.533 --> 00:09:07.700
- Tony, it's just been locked
up inside of me forever.

00:09:08.982 --> 00:09:12.562
I've had a speech impediment,
I've stuttered my entire life.

00:09:12.562 --> 00:09:15.979
Guys, 30 years of stuttering, stammering,

00:09:17.288 --> 00:09:21.073
but that was a condition that I chose.

00:09:21.073 --> 00:09:23.065
I chose to stay there.

00:09:23.065 --> 00:09:26.276
I chose to identify as a stutterer.

00:09:26.276 --> 00:09:29.327
That's why I was afraid of greatness.

00:09:29.327 --> 00:09:32.211
I was afraid of my light shining.

00:09:32.211 --> 00:09:35.878
But, no more. Because
today, I am the voice.

00:09:37.654 --> 00:09:39.973
Today, I am the warrior.

00:09:39.973 --> 00:09:42.454
Today, lives will be changed.

00:09:42.454 --> 00:09:45.454
Today, I saw this moment as a child.

00:09:46.888 --> 00:09:49.817
I knew that I would be on stage talking

00:09:49.817 --> 00:09:51.694
to countless of thousands of people.

00:09:51.694 --> 00:09:54.909
Thank you for the pain.
Thank you for the obstacles.

00:09:54.909 --> 00:09:58.932
Because that brought me
here today to talk to you,

00:09:58.932 --> 00:10:02.021
to give you my story, to give you me.

00:10:02.021 --> 00:10:05.104
Now you got me, I got you, and do it.

00:10:06.012 --> 00:10:09.012
(audience applause)

00:10:45.979 --> 00:10:47.934
- Thank you guys so much for
watching. I hope you enjoyed.

00:10:47.934 --> 00:10:49.849
I'd love to know have
you seen this video yet?

00:10:49.849 --> 00:10:51.314
If not, did you like it?

00:10:51.314 --> 00:10:53.390
If you've seen it already,
did you like it too?

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:56.030
Let me know your comments,
leave it down there below.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:57.291
I'm really curious to find out.

00:10:57.291 --> 00:10:59.569
This is also an experimental series,

00:10:59.569 --> 00:11:01.729
this Best of Tony series on this channel,

00:11:01.729 --> 00:11:04.047
so if you want it to
continue, let me know.

00:11:04.047 --> 00:11:06.077
Leave it below, share the video up.

00:11:06.077 --> 00:11:09.086
If this series has the
impact that I'm looking for,

00:11:09.086 --> 00:11:10.269
then we'll continue.

00:11:10.269 --> 00:11:11.575
If not, we'll find something else.

00:11:11.575 --> 00:11:13.688
Your viewership makes a big difference

00:11:13.688 --> 00:11:16.087
in the deciding factor here.

00:11:16.087 --> 00:11:18.082
So thank you guys for watching,
I hope you enjoyed it.

00:11:18.082 --> 00:11:20.243
I believe in you. I hope you continue

00:11:20.243 --> 00:11:23.785
to believe in yourself, and
whatever your one word is.

00:11:23.785 --> 00:11:26.202
Much love. I'll see you soon.

